{{New unreviewed article|source=ArticleWizard|date=April 2011}}
[[Image:Shitori.jpg|thumb|right|300px|Shitori Jinja in [[Yurihama, Tottori|Yurihama]]]]
{{nihongo|'''Shitori Jinja'''|倭文神社}} is a [[Shinto shrine]] in [[Yurihama, Tottori|Yurihama]], [[Tottori Prefecture]], [[Japan]]. Artefacts from the sutra burial ground (1103) have been designated a [[National Treasures of Japan|National Treasure]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.bunka.go.jp/bsys/maindetails.asp?register_id=201&item_id=845 |title=Database of Registered National Cultural Properties |publisher=[[Agency for Cultural Affairs]] |accessdate=23 April 2011}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.pref.tottori.lg.jp/dd.aspx?menuid=100979 |title=Shitori sutra mound |publisher=[[Tottori Prefecture]] |accessdate=23 April 2011}}</ref>
==See also== * [[Modern system of ranked Shinto Shrines]] * [[List of National Treasures of Japan (archaeological materials)]]
==References== {{Reflist}}
