{{nihongo|'''Shitori Shrine'''|倭文神社}} is a {{ill|Shinto shrine|8=en}} in the Miyauchi neighborhood of the town of {{ill|Yurihama, Tottori|Yurihama|8=en}} in {{ill|Tottori Prefecture|8=en}}, {{ill|Japan|8=en}}, on the east bank of {{ill|Lake Tōgō|8=en}}. It is the ''{{ill|ichinomiya|8=en}}'' of former {{ill|Hōki Province|8=en}}. The main festival of the shrine is held annually on 1 May.<ref>{{cite book |last1=Shibuya |first1=Nobuhiro |title=Shokoku jinja Ichinomiya Ninomiya San'nomiya |date=2015 |publisher= Yamakawa shuppansha |isbn=978-4634150867 |language=Japanese}}</ref> 

==Enshrined ''kami''==
