{{nihongo|'''Shitori Shrine'''|倭文神社}} is a {{ill|Shinto shrine|8=en|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shinto shrine|qq=}} in the Miyauchi neighborhood of the town of {{ill|Yurihama, Tottori|lt=Yurihama|8=en|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yurihama, Tottori|qq=}} in {{ill|Tottori Prefecture|8=en|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Tottori Prefecture|qq=}}, {{ill|Japan|8=en|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Japan|qq=}}, on the east bank of {{ill|Lake Tōgō|8=en|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Lake Tōgō|qq=}}. It is the ''{{ill|ichinomiya|8=en|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/ichinomiya|qq=}}'' of former {{ill|Hōki Province|8=en|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hōki Province|qq=}}. The main festival of the shrine is held annually on 1 May.<ref>{{cite book|last1=Shibuya |first1=Nobuhiro |title=Shokoku jinja Ichinomiya Ninomiya San'nomiya |date=2015 |publisher= Yamakawa shuppansha |isbn=978-4634150867 |language=Japanese|qq=draft|qq=draft}}</ref> 

==Enshrined ''kami''==
